\begin_layout Standard
The SEED and SEED-V datasets, detailed in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "SEED_1,SEED_2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "SEED-V_1"
literal "false"

\end_inset

, are comprehensive EEG-based emotion recognition datasets utilized in this
 research.
 Both datasets consist of EEG data collected using a 62-channel ESI NeuroScan
 System and were downsampled to 200 Hz.
 Preprocessing for both datasets involved bandpass filtering (0-75 Hz for
 SEED, 1-75 Hz for SEED-V) to remove noise and artifacts.
 Eye-tracking data were collected using SMI eye-tracking glasses.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
SEED
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The SEED dataset, as described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "SEED_1,SEED_2"
literal "false"

\end_inset

, includes data from 15 Chinese subjects who participated in experiments
 designed to elicit positive, neutral, or negative emotions through 15 carefully
 selected film clips.
 The EEG data was collected and downsampled to 200 Hz.
 Preprocessing involved bandpass filtering (0-75 Hz) and segmenting the
 data to match the duration of each film clip, resulting in 45 files per
 subject.
 Each subject underwent three experimental sessions, spaced approximately
 one week apart, yielding data arrays corresponding to each of the 15 trials
 per session.
 The dataset also provides extracted features such as differential entropy
 (DE), differential asymmetry (DASM), and rational asymmetry (RASM), along
 with smoothed versions of these features.
 The SEED_Multimodal part includes raw EEG data, DE features, and eye-tracking
 data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For our purposes, only the preprocessed EEG data from the SEED_EEG part
 was utilized.
 This approach excludes the generated features (DE, DASM, RASM) and the
 multimodal components, focusing solely on the preprocessed, segmented EEG
 signals for emotion recognition research.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
SEED-V
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The SEED-V dataset, detailed in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand citep
key "SEED-V_1"
literal "false"

\end_inset

, includes data from 20 subjects (10 males and 10 females) from Shanghai
 Jiao Tong University.
 Each subject participated in the experiment three times, with at least
 three days between sessions, watching 15 film clips per session designed
 to elicit specific emotions: happiness, neutrality, sadness, disgust, and
 fear.
 The EEG data were downsampled to a 200 Hz sampling rate and processed with
 a bandpass filter between 1 Hz and 75 Hz.
 Differential entropy (DE) features were extracted across five frequency
 bands (delta, theta, alpha, beta, gamma).
 Eye movement features were also collected, including parameters such as
 pupil diameter, fixation, saccade, and blink.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For our purposes, only the preprocessed EEG data from SEED-V was utilized,
 specifically the raw EEG signals that had been downsampled and passed through
 a bandpass filter.
 This approach excludes the use of extracted features such as differential
 entropy (DE) and the eye movement data, ensuring a streamlined focus on
 the bandpass-filtered EEG signals for emotion recognition research.
\end_layout

