\begin_layout Subsection
Participant and Experimental Setup
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This study involved the creation of a custom dataset, hereafter referred
 to as EmotionWave, which involved a single participant, the researcher,
 who collected the data.
 The participant underwent three separate sessions, each conducted on different
 days with at least three days between sessions.
 Each session consisted of 15 trials, with each trial designed to elicit
 one of three emotions: positive, negative, or neutral.
 The EEG data were processed with a bandpass filter ranging from 0.5 Hz to
 75 Hz and downsampled from the original 256 Hz to 200 Hz using polyphase
 filtering.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Overall, after segmenting the EEG data into 1-second windows with dimensions
 
\begin_inset Formula $14\times200$
\end_inset

, the dataset comprises 5760 EEG segments.
 Each segment represents a 1-second snapshot of the brain's activity during
 the emotional elicitation trials, providing a rich dataset for further
 analysis and model training.
\end_layout

