\series bold
5s Self-Assessment: 
\series default
Following the viewing of each film clip, the participant conducted a self-assess
ment to rate their emotional reaction.
 They used a scale from 1 to 10, where a rating near 10 indicated that the
 emotion was strongly conveyed and felt (e.g., feeling happy after a positive
 video), while a rating near 1 indicated the opposite.
 For neutral stimuli, a score of 10 was given if the participant's mood
 remained unchanged, and a score of 1 if their mood fluctuated.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
15s Rest: 
\series default
The participant was given a 15-second rest period in which they were instructed
 to close their eyes until the next hint appeared.
 This ensured a clear transition and preparation for the subsequent stimulus.
\end_layout

