Reference Points:
\series default
 Two reference points, CMS/DRL (located at P3/P4), and alternative reference
 points at the left/right mastoid process are used for grounding and noise
 reduction.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Sampling Rate:
\series default
 The original sampling rate was set to 256 Hz, providing high-resolution
 EEG data.
 This rate was chosen to capture the fine-grained electrical activity of
 the brain accurately.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Connectivity:
\series default
 Data was transmitted using the extender in pass-through mode.
 This setup involved connecting the headset to the extender, which was then
 connected to the PC via USB.
 The extender increased the battery life of the headset, allowing for continuous
 recording during longer sessions without the need for frequent recharging.
 This method ensured minimal movement constraints and facilitated a comfortable
 environment for the participant during the data collection sessions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Sensor Material:
\series default
 The headset uses saline-soaked felt pads for sensors, ensuring good conductivit
y and reducing skin impedance.
 This material choice helps in obtaining cleaner EEG signals with minimal
 artifacts.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Internal Filtering:
\series default
 The EMOTIV EPOC X has built-in digital notch filters at 50Hz and 60Hz to
 eliminate power line interference, which is critical for maintaining data
 quality during recording.
\end_layout

