\begin_layout Standard
The fine-tuning phase of our model was conducted using the SEED dataset,
 with the evaluation being carried out on 30% of the dataset, stratified
 for the verdicts of the EEG data.
 The overall fine-tuning process took approximately 9 hours.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:finetuning-seed-train-loss"

\end_inset

 depicts the training loss per epoch.
 The training loss decreases consistently throughout the training process,
 reaching a minimum of 2.7832 at epoch 20.
 The continuous decrease in training loss indicates effective learning and
 optimization of the model parameters during fine-tuning.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:finetuning-seed-eval-loss"

\end_inset

 shows the evaluation loss per epoch.
 Initially, the evaluation loss decreases significantly, reaching a minimum
 value of 3.2316 at epoch 13.
 However, after epoch 13, the evaluation loss starts to show slight fluctuations
, potentially indicating the model's performance on the evaluation dataset
 has started to stabilize.
 The final evaluation loss at epoch 20 is 3.3179, representing an overall
 increase of 0.0863 from the minimum value observed.
 To avoid overfitting, the training was halted at this point.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:finetuning-seed-eval-accuracy"

\end_inset

 illustrates the evaluation accuracy per epoch.
 The evaluation accuracy shows a consistent upward trend, starting from
 50.78% and peaking at around 74% starting with epoch 13.
 Although there are slight fluctuations in accuracy after epoch 13, the
 overall trend indicates that the model maintains a high level of accuracy
 on the evaluation dataset.
 The highest accuracy of 74.13% reflects an overall improvement of 23.35%
 from the initial accuracy, which was derived from the pre-trained model.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The steady decrease in both training and evaluation losses, combined with
 the increase in evaluation accuracy, demonstrates the effectiveness of
 the fine-tuning process.
 The fluctuations in evaluation loss and accuracy post-epoch 13 could be
 attributed to the model reaching its capacity to generalize on the validation
 set, indicating a balance between fitting the training data and maintaining
 performance on the evaluation set.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These results underscore the importance of fine-tuning in enhancing the
 model's performance, particularly in adapting pre-trained models to specific
 datasets.
 The stratified evaluation ensures that the model's performance metrics
 are reliable and representative of its generalization capability across
 different classes in the EEG data.
\end_layout

