 shows the loss for the discriminator over epochs.
 The discriminator's loss decreases and stabilizes after about 250 epochs,
 indicating that it effectively learns to distinguish between real and synthetic
 EEG signals early in the training process.
 This stability suggests that the discriminator quickly adapts to its task
 and maintains a robust performance throughout the training.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
