 synthetic data that can consistently deceive the discriminator.
 This is further evidenced by the loss plateauing after the initial learning
 rate reduction, implying that the generator does not gain additional improvemen
ts in generating realistic EEG data despite the adjusted learning rate.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These results highlight a disparity in the learning dynamics between the
 generator and discriminator.
 While the discriminator adapts quickly and maintains stability, the generator
 faces challenges in optimizing its performance.
 This indicates the need for a more balanced learning rate strategy or additiona
l training techniques to enhance the generator's capability to produce high-qual
ity synthetic EEG data.
