\begin_layout Section
Summary of Findings
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Summary of Findings"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This research introduced the EmotionWave dataset, created using the EMOTIV
 EPOC X headset, to address the challenges in EEG-based emotion recognition.
 By leveraging the Joint Contrastive Learning framework with Feature Alignment
 (JCFA) and incorporating GAN-based data augmentation, the study aimed to
 enhance model performance.
 The comparative analysis between the SEED and EmotionWave datasets revealed
 that while pre-training with GAN-augmented data initially showed promise,
 the highest evaluation accuracy was achieved with a model pre-trained without
 GAN data, but fine-tuned with GAN data, achieving a peak accuracy of 66.45%.
 The SEED dataset consistently outperformed the EmotionWave dataset in terms
 of stability and peak accuracy during fine-tuning, underscoring the importance
 of dataset quality and optimization strategies.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Contributions
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Contributions"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This thesis makes several contributions to the field of EEG-based emotion
 recognition:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The development of the EmotionWave dataset, tailored specifically for emotion
 recognition with the EPOC X headset, providing a new resource for future
 research.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The implementation of GANs for effective data augmentation, which increased
 the dataset's size and diversity, demonstrating the potential of GANs in
 addressing data scarcity and variability.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The adaptation of the JCFA framework for the 14-channel EEG configuration
 of the EPOC X, showcasing the framework's flexibility and applicability
 to different EEG setups.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Detailed experimentation and analysis, demonstrating the impact of GAN-augmented
 data on model performance and providing insights into the complexities
 introduced by such augmentation.
\end_layout

